# Generated Flatpak stubs run as plain untrusted apps. They are signed with a
# device-generated key, so no build-time seinfo can name them, and libselinux
# rejects a name-only rule for non-privileged apps (insecure: any app could take
# a flatpak.* name), failing the whole file and leaving every app in zygote.
# linuxd and the System Bridge verify the stub certificate themselves.

